.TH VIBEMIN 1 "2026-08-18" "vibemin 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
vibemin \- minimize an AI-generated Git diff under executable constraints
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibemin
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ path ... ]
.B \-c
.I command
.RI [ \-c
.IR command ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vibemin
uses delta debugging to remove inserted and deleted lines from the
difference between a Git baseline and the working tree.  A smaller
candidate is retained only when every verification command succeeds.
.PP
Candidates run in a disposable detached worktree.  The real checkout is
changed only after a verified result has been found.  Text lines are
independent reduction units; binary and empty-file changes are atomic.
.PP
The result is minimal only with respect to the supplied commands and
existing diff units.  It does not synthesize a globally shortest
implementation.  Weak checks can accept incorrect reductions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Run a non-mutating test, lint, formatter-check, typecheck, security check,
or other oracle.  This option is required and may be repeated.  Commands
run from the temporary repository root.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-preserve-output " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Capture the successful command's stdout and stderr for the original
candidate and require every smaller candidate to reproduce it exactly.
Use only deterministic commands.  This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-final-check " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Run an expensive clean-install, dependency audit, or broad validation once
on the selected final candidate.  This option may be repeated.
.TP
.BR \-\-security-check " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Add a security-specific oracle.  Required when reducible files contain auth,
tenant, permission, session, token, cookie, or secret concerns.
.TP
.BR \-\-test-strength-check " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Add a mutation or equivalent test-strength oracle.  Required to unlock test
changes unless deterministic collection output is preserved.
.TP
.BR \-\-dependency-check " " \fICOMMAND\fR
Add a manifest/lock consistency oracle.  Required to unlock dependency files.
.TP
.BR \--allow-test-changes ", " \--reduce-tests
Allow test/spec/snapshot reduction with a test-strength guard.
.TP
.B \--allow-dependency-changes
Allow dependency manifest or lockfile reduction with a dependency guard.
.TP
.B \--allow-visual-changes
Allow stylesheet or visual-asset reduction with deterministic preserved output.
.TP
.B \--allow-untyped-typescript
Explicitly permit TypeScript reduction without tsc/typecheck.  This weakens the
default safety policy and is not recommended.
.TP
.BR \-\-base " " \fIREF\fR
Compare the working tree with the exact commit or ref instead of HEAD.
.TP
.BR \-\-feature-base " " \fIREF\fR
Minimize the complete current feature since the merge-base of HEAD and REF.
Committed feature changes are included; the result is left as working-tree
changes ready to amend or squash.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Set the maximum duration of each command.  The default is 300 seconds.
.TP
.BR \-\-max-attempts " " \fIN\fR
Stop after at most N candidate checks.  The default is 500.
.TP
.B \--dry-run
Find and report the reduction without changing the real checkout.
.TP
.B \--verbose
Print the captured output of failed verification commands.
.TP
.B \-h, \--help
Show command help and exit.
.SH ALGORITHM
The initial changed-line set must pass every check.  Vibemin then removes
progressively smaller groups of diff units.  A passing candidate becomes
the new working set.  When allowed to finish, the result is 1-minimal: no
remaining individual unit was demonstrated removable by the supplied
oracles.
.SH MINIMIZING PRODUCTION CODE
Scope reduction to implementation paths and leave tests as fixed context:
.PP
.nf
vibemin src/excel.py \
  --check "pytest -q tests/test_excel.py" \
  --check "ruff check src/excel.py" \
  --check "ruff format --check src/excel.py"
.fi
.PP
Tests/specs/snapshots, dependency manifests/lockfiles, and visual styles/assets
are fixed context by default.  TypeScript changes require a typecheck.  Security-
sensitive changes require a security-specific oracle.  Protected categories can
only be unlocked with their corresponding options and guards.
.SH MINIMIZING TEST CODE
A passing suite alone is not a sufficient oracle for reducing tests:
deleting a test makes the suite easier to pass.  When simplifying test
bodies without changing test cases, preserve the collection inventory:
.PP
.nf
vibemin tests/excel \
  --reduce-tests \
  --check "pytest -q tests/excel" \
  --preserve-output \
  "pytest --collect-only -q tests/excel | sed '/collected in/d'"
.fi
.PP
When intentionally merging or deleting redundant cases, require a
mutation-testing command that preserves the baseline mutation score or,
preferably, the exact killed-mutant set.  Line or branch coverage alone
does not preserve assertion strength.
.SH SAFETY
Staged changes are rejected.  Verification commands that modify candidate
files are rejected.  Changed symlinks, directories, and submodules are
unsupported.  Tests, dependency metadata, and unobserved visual changes are
protected by default.  The original checkout is checked for concurrent changes
before applying the result.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIBEMIN_ROOT
Set for verification commands to the temporary worktree root.
.SH LIMITATIONS
Ignored files such as .env, .venv, and node_modules are not copied to the
temporary worktree.  Commands must use available dependencies or shared
package-manager caches.  Always review the final diff and rerun the
relevant suite in the real checkout.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero on success; 2 for invalid usage, Git safety failures, or an original
candidate that does not pass its verification commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.claude/skills/vibemin/SKILL.md
Recommended location for the user-wide Claude Code skill.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-diff (1),
.BR pytest (1)
